Description: Let the key none switch a binding off
 Regolith's shipped bindings take their keys from trawl resources, as in
 "bindsym $mod+$wm.binding.terminal exec ...", so the natural way to drop
 one is to set its resource to none. sway rejected that with "Unknown key
 or button 'none'", and swaynag reported it on every start and reload.
 .
 A bindsym, bindcode, unbindsym or unbindcode key combination that
 contains the key none, in any letter case, is now accepted and does
 nothing: no binding is added or removed and nothing is logged above
 debug level. Every other key in the combination is still checked, so a
 typo such as Mod4+Retrun+none is still reported as an unknown key.
 Because nothing is bound, any number of such lines may share the same
 modifiers without "Overwriting binding" warnings. sway(5) documents the
 behaviour.
