+	If _key combo_ contains the key _none_ (in any letter case), nothing is
+	bound and no warning is given, provided the other keys in _key combo_ are
+	valid. A binding whose key is taken from a variable can therefore be
+	switched off by setting the variable to _none_. *bindcode*, *unbindsym*
+	and *unbindcode* handle _none_ in the same way; the latter two remove
+	nothing.
